-- title:
--   Even-weight dimension lower bound for M_k(Γ₁(M))
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive integer with $M \ge 5$, and let $k$ be a natural number with $3 \le k$ and $k$ even. The assertion is that there exist a natural number $d$ and a family $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to \mathrm{ModularForm}\,(\Gamma_1(M))\,k$ of modular forms of weight $k$ (the integer cast of $k$) for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(M) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, linearly independent over $\mathbb{C}$, such that
--   $$(k-1)\,\big[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_1(M)\,\sqcup\,\langle -1\rangle\big] \;+\; 6\,\#\big(\Gamma_1(M)\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\langle T, -1\rangle\big) \;\le\; 12\,d .$$
--   Here the first index is the index, as a natural number, of the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ generated by $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with $-1$ (the join of $\Gamma_1(M)$ with the subgroup of integer powers of $-1$); $k-1$ is truncated subtraction of naturals, harmless since $k \ge 3$; and the second term counts the double cosets of $\Gamma_1(M)$ and of the subgroup generated by the translation matrix $T$ and $-1$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, as the cardinality of the corresponding double coset quotient. Thus $\dim_{\mathbb{C}} M_k(\Gamma_1(M)) \ge d$ is bounded below by one twelfth of the displayed expression.
--
--   This is the even-weight case of the classical lower bound on the dimension of the space of weight-$k$ modular forms on $\Gamma_1(M)$, the right-hand side of the classical dimension formula for $M \ge 5$ (no elliptic points, all cusps regular) being written in terms of the index of $\pm\Gamma_1(M)$ and the number of cusps presented as a double coset count. It is combined with the odd-weight case in [`ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card`](thm.html#ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card), which supplies the supply of forms needed later in the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularForm_exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card_of_even.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X1

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open CongruenceSubgroup ModularCurve
open scoped MatrixGroups ModularForm

theorem ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card_of_even
    (M : ℕ) [NeZero M] (hM : 5 ≤ M) (k : ℕ) (hk : 3 ≤ k) (hke : Even k) :
    ∃ (d : ℕ) (f : Fin d → ModularForm (Gamma1 M) (k : ℤ)), LinearIndependent ℂ f ∧
      (k - 1) * (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 M ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers (-1 : SL(2, ℤ))).index +
          6 * Nat.card (DoubleCoset.Quotient (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 M : Set SL(2, ℤ))
            ((Subgroup.zpowers ModularGroup.T ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers (-1) : Subgroup SL(2, ℤ)) : Set SL(2, ℤ)))
        ≤ 12 * d := by sorry
